(2) A member of a household shall be engaged in work if such member is participating in the work activities listed in paragraph (3) of this subdivision for at least the number of hours per week, averaged monthly, as specified in subparagraphs (i) through (iii) of this paragraph, provided, however, that a recipient who is the only parent or caretaker relative in the family of a child who has not attained six years of age is deemed to be engaged in work for a month if the recipient is engaged in work for an average of at least 20 hours per week during the month:
